WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.950
(October, the 14th of Shinka Era
 Indian Ocean)

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:12.620
Maria!

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:14.160
Move, Maria.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.330
I have orders from
 the Imperial Government.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:28.580
GaGon!

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.790
GaGon.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.450
That's the islanders' word
 for "big human."

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.290
It has the characteristics of
 a Gigantopithecus giganteus.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.530
(August, the 17th of Shinka Era
 U.S. Joint Staff Pacific Headquarters)

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.040
Now you know.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.580
Why we have to throw
 the superhuman in the frontline.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.160
(November, the 29th of Shinka Era
 Tokyo)

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:23.000
We saw it, a huge beast!

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.100
We all saw it.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.020
A beast? But where?

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.040
Jiro!

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:49.660
Emi! What did you do?

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:50.670
Nothing.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.120
You brought him out here.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.170
Come down and help.

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.790
What are you doing
 at a time like this?

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:10.440
I like this.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:35.290
Concrete Revolutio
 ~Superhuman Phantasmagoria~

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:42.450
I heard it
 A voice cursing fate

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:46.660
I found it
 A way to use my power

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:50.200
What you want are not words,
 are they?

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:53.870
That love inside
 I want to send it on

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.610
Justice is not on my side

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.570
The only thing absolute for me
 is myself

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.410
Come on Wakers. Ready, go!

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:08.620
Protecting the illusions
 that somebody dreamed of

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:12.870
will liberate the stagnant sky

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:18.700
We hurl our unanswerable cries
 at each other

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:23.660
And they become the reason we live

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:29.370
What can I do in this
 hopeless world we live in?

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:33.870
Only those that keep searching

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:37.200
can become the future

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:41.120
Start the revolution!

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.000
(January, the 41st of Shinka Era
 Superhuman Bureau)

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.200
Hello.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.880
What? A huge creature in the lake?

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:59.120
It's in Fukushima.
 A little far, but can you go?

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.660
If I can use my car.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:04.120
Don't get found out.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:07.290
The little boy's car
 still needs a little tuning.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.290
Sorry.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:10.250
A beast.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:13.660
If damage might spread, may I attack?

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:18.040
Our job is solely to protect
 and control superhumans.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:20.910
Don't forget that
 and get hotheaded.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:21.910
That's hot!

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.540
This is a monster too, right?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.950
That's right.
 Monsters are on the human's side.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.080
And that...

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.250
The bad beast.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:41.410
I can't let it run free.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:44.290
What's wrong?
 Getting worked up like that.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:46.870
Let's attack. Lend me a hand.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.750
That's only a last resort.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.250
We don't know if it's evil yet.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.600
Impossible. All beasts are evil.

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:56.620
You mean, for humans.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.480
You're so cute.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.540
What? There was another one?

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.040
No, I don't think so.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:21.250
What's going on?

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:22.910
Those two are close by.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:26.550
But we can't see them.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.290
It's the Fred and Hoyle effect.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.410
They transitioned
 to an adjacent dimension.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.330
What should we do?

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:36.040
The second one is
 an unidentified superhuman.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:37.540
We can't do anything.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.270
We don't need science but magic.

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:44.780
How about we call it Grosse Augen?

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.870
That means "big eye," right?

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:51.200
He has a huge eye
 in the middle of his body.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:00.840
And so, Grosse Augen debuted on Earth
 as a beast-eradicating superhuman.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:08.040
But as you know,
 he couldn't stay on Earth and left.

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:13.700
And that was how I, Kikko Hoshino,
 joined the Superhuman Bureau.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:17.890
It's been a month since
 Grosse Augen vanished from Earth.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.770
He won't come back.

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:23.290
Will he?

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:27.290
He abandoned his host's body
 and returned to his planet.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:29.030
He'll never come back.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:32.580
The problem is how to
 handle beasts from now on.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:37.160
There are hardly any other
 huge superhumans like Grosse Augen.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.000
I have Equus.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:43.330
The Bureau's goal isn't to fight.

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:45.500
It's to secretly manage superhumans.

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:47.250
And protect them.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.430
- Excuse me.
 - Yes Kikko?

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:54.060
I have a question
 after hearing all this.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:59.290
Why are beasts killed
 without question?

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.200
I'm coming.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:04.200
Hello?

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:06.200
What? A beast appeared?

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:15.750
I'm scared.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:17.580
Somebody, do something!

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.290
This is why.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.330
Their very existence is dangerous.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:26.540
But there must be
 a reason they were born.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.700
Like losing their habitat
 or falling from space.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:34.410
Many Japanese fishing ships were
 wrecked in last year's Typhoon No. 29.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.290
Over 200 people are still missing.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.830
If that typhoon was caused by a beast,

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:43.270
you'd say we should've
 killed it earlier.

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:46.900
So beasts are the same as
 typhoons and earthquakes?

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:58.410
- Should I lock it?
 - Yeah.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.660
I'll get rid of that beast.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:06.160
We can't use your machine
 with all these people watching.

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:08.950
There's a limit to media censoring.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:13.950
Aren't there other superhumans like
 Grosse Augen that'll fight beasts?

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:17.540
Each superhuman has
 its own evil to fight.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:20.160
- Not just beasts...
 - It's Earth-chan!

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:23.060
- Where?
 - Over there!

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:32.000
A superhuman that's
 been around over 10 years.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.290
One of the oldies.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:34.750
Is it a robot?

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.500
I told you it was too early to use it.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:53.250
But it's just started.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:55.970
You'll still help out, won't you?

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:06.250
The robbers that Earth-chan was after
 were controlling the beast.

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:08.900
Everybody knows about Earth-chan.

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:11.790
But it's not in the papers or news.

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:15.580
It's against the law to
 report about superhumans.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:18.750
So that's why it's only in tabloids.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:21.740
But this is all lies, too.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.910
We make them do that.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.580
That's the Superhuman Bureau's
 job too?

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:30.790
Superhumans are easily misunderstood.

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:34.750
That's why we have to
 hide and protect them.

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:36.630
But...

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:40.000
So that they don't
 have to hide forever,

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:43.160
a Bureau like ours is made.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:48.200
Hoshinoko. We might've been
 a little hasty in joining them.

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:51.620
By the way, Miss Emi.
 Where were you yesterday?

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:54.290
I'm Prof. Hitoyoshi's assistant too.

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:56.530
Hitoyoshi...?

00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.370
My foster father.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:05.250
As if they'd been waiting
 for Grosse Augen to disappear,

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:09.000
the number of rampaging beasts
 rose rapidly around that time.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.200
(Another monster!)

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:11.540
(Countermeasure talks started)

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:12.500
(Protests demanding action)

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:16.910
But none of the beasts
 really caused much damage.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:19.540
Because...

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:21.930
Fight, Gigander Seven!

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.290
As the number of beasts increased,

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:32.200
Superhumans that had been laying low
 and new superhumans

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:34.910
stood up and came to the rescue.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:39.000
Plus, there were rumors of
 a certain superhuman.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:51.290
Climbers claimed that what killed
 two beasts was a huge superhuman.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.750
(November, the 41st of Shinka Era
 Kamata)

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.500
Gross Augen went back to space.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:01.930
You saw it too.

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.250
But this rapid increase of beasts.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:08.810
Isn't it related to
 Grosse Augen leaving?

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:11.580
I don't know.

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:13.450
Are we there yet, Fuurouta?

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:18.540
Think he'll eat it?

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:20.580
He'll eat anything.

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:22.280
That's amazing.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:26.450
Hey, if you let him eat that,
 it'll make GaGon stupid.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:28.580
Hey!

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.870
Oh, it's Fuurouta.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:33.700
Hiroyuki, let me see that thing
 you told me about.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.840
You're a ghost and
 want to see a beast?

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.960
Ghosts are so yesterday.

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:43.790
It's so cute!

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.470
This is the beast?

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:47.370
Who are they?

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:48.970
They're good guys.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:51.040
They're pros at this stuff.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:54.730
Wow, a beast professor?

00:11:56.410 --> 00:12:01.200
What are you going to do?
 You can't just step on him with Equus.

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:05.040
Excuse me.
 Are you from the Superhuman Bureau?

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:19.290
I've heard rumors.

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:22.930
An institution solely for
 superhuman cases.

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:25.660
Um, what is this company?

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:27.680
We want to do a late night broadcast.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:30.830
Radio DJs are popular these days.

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:33.950
So I want to do a show
 that specializes on beasts.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:35.810
That's why it's "Radio Wave."

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:37.980
I'm the president, Matsumoto.

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:40.580
Beasts are popular.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:43.860
Not just with kids,
 but with young people like me.

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:47.620
So if a beast appears,
 I want to report it live.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:51.950
I'm consulting ad agencies about
 making a program like that.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:53.580
And this factory?

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.660
All my father left me was
 this and some debt.

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:59.500
I couldn't go to college and
 had to make a living like this.

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:02.260
So make it big with the beast radio?

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:04.580
Well, that too.

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:07.260
But I feel sorry for the beasts.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:08.700
Feel sorry?

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:11.450
Humans are what created beasts.

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:16.160
They're born from wars, experiments,
 and even industrial waste.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:20.520
Humans made them, so humans
 should think about coexisting.

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:24.250
No, beasts were created from nature.

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:27.410
Can humans coexist with
 volcanoes and earthquakes?

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:29.250
We already do.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.660
We live on volcanic islands,

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:35.660
and can't run
 from earthquakes or typhoons.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:41.500
And what about the little beast?

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:45.260
GaGon is Hiroyuki's little brother.

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:46.910
Little brother?

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:51.760
7 years ago, when a beast appeared
 in Tokyo and caused great damage...

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:54.790
(January, the 34th of Shinka Era
 Tokyo)

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:14.080
Darn it... Darn it!

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:20.160
The beast Giganto Gon was controlled
 by an international conspiracy ring.

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:22.790
It was killed by the superhuman
 Rainbow Knight.

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:49.040
The homeless Hiroyuki had a brother
 who died from malnutrition.

00:14:49.790 --> 00:14:54.000
To him, the baby beast was like
 a reincarnation of his brother.

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:59.620
He's really gentle and
 hasn't grown in years.

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:04.200
Seeing them, I know
 humans and beasts can get along.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.160
Winner, GaGon!

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:08.500
I believe it too.
 Right, Senpai?

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:11.660
Let me consult my superiors once.

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:15.720
Why are you here?

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:18.350
And you, Mr. Detective?

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:23.450
The crime lab analyzed the dead bodies
 of the recurring beasts.

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:26.610
It's not clear,
 but the cells are similar.

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:28.490
What do you mean?

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:32.040
Meaning somebody could be
 breeding the beasts,

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:36.370
and selling them
 to crime syndicates all over.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:40.870
There was a report that
 there were beast lovers here.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.700
See for yourself.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.830
You can't breed beasts here.

00:15:45.870 --> 00:15:48.950
They're just a bunch
 of beast groupies.

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:54.080
There are lots of superhumans
 battling beasts these days.

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:57.330
What are you conspiring?

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:01.910
Conspire? Are you really a detective?

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.560
Yeah, I am.

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:07.020
Specializing in superhuman crimes.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:16.450
Somebody's making beasts appear
 to make superhumans look good.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:18.370
Or that's what rumor says.

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:20.120
Are you being serious?

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:25.250
Thank you for keeping GaGon a secret.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:26.200
It's nothing.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:29.660
So you didn't hate beasts after all.

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:32.080
I just hate that detective even more.

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:36.550
He may be harmless now,
 but I'll come check occasionally.

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.410
So we'll meet again.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:48.410
What, you like him GaGon?

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:50.870
He's hardly ever like this.

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:53.450
Let go. I said, let go!

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:59.290
The beasts kept appearing.
 And so did the superhumans.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:03.580
Around that time, shocking news
 reached us from overseas.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:04.830
(Master Ultima back from Mars)

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.210
(Tomorrow, press conference
 broadcast live across the globe)

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:13.340
President Uchihata.
 And Shimazu is here too.

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:16.750
We three haven't met in a while.

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:21.660
Is it about Master Ultima?

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:24.230
Things are about to get messy.

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.950
Talking like this is too sluggish.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:29.730
Let's be open.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:41.750
Military use of beasts?

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.370
They've captured this space beast.

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:45.410
The White House's ace
 against the Soviet.

00:17:45.450 --> 00:17:47.450
It's a weapon of justice.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:50.500
Our government wouldn't follow suit.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:54.290
But stop the heroic superhumans
 beating evil beasts act.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:56.080
We don't want the US army coming.

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:58.870
The police are investigating
 the beast trade.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:01.950
I can't stop them unless you cut ties.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.500
I thought it was a good idea though.

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:10.700
To make society learn of superhumans,

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:13.040
we need a clear-cut evil force.

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:15.650
Companies and countries
 can be good and evil.

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:19.160
But beasts are evil to everyone.

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:25.410
Strangely, some people of this planet
 tend to love these harmful beasts.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:29.080
Seems like there's
 a beast craze going on.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:34.670
13 beasts that have appeared
 since last autumn

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:39.800
have all been sold to
 each organization by the same maker.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:43.250
So Detective Shiba's guess was right.

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:46.810
They've been supplying enemies
 for the superhumans.

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:51.980
We'll make it so none of it had
 happened. The ministry has agreed.

00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:56.110
The broker was
 Beastly Radio Wave Japan Inc.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:58.290
Senpai!

00:18:58.330 --> 00:19:00.240
That can't be.

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.120
Senpai!

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:14.120
Ms. Ukyo!

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:17.000
- What have you guys done?
 - I'm sorry.

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:20.120
We've done something beyond repair.

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:26.620
We cultivated real beasts
 using bits of GaGon.

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:28.200
The president...

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:31.690
There's a path to the basement.
 Here's the key.

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:37.450
Hurry up, Ms. Ukyo.

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:39.250
Matsumoto!

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:41.830
What have you been doing here?

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:44.070
The Superhuman Bureau! Why?

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:50.330
What are you doing?

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:56.460
What? Beasts are anger.
 Mine. Human's.

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.660
Go, Big GaGon!

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:16.290
Beast...

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:26.160
Lock one.

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:29.580
Lock two.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:34.500
Lock three.

00:21:22.580 --> 00:21:24.170
Miss Emi.

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:28.050
It's okay, Jiro. It's okay.

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:52.790
Big Sis Ukyo...

00:22:13.620 --> 00:22:14.810
Emi...

00:23:56.910 --> 00:24:01.660
You all know that beasts
 aren't just big and scary, right?

00:24:01.700 --> 00:24:05.630
The jolly beast GaGon
 will come to your town soon.

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:08.450
He'll be happy after eating
 dumplings and rice.

00:24:08.500 --> 00:24:10.660
GaGon is your little brother.
